  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/... \n\nThe long term forecast remains dry and seasonal. There is now\nmuch better confidence in the late week and weekend forecast,\nwhich favors ridging building in across the West and a weak cutoff\nlow forming over the Pacific west of Baja California. Weak\ntroughing looks to drag across the local area Friday into Saturday\nahead of the building ridge. Previous forecasts supported slight \nrain chances with this trough, but this trough now looks\ncompletely dry and latest NBM PoPs are 5% or less across the\nregion. These are also the only PoPs in the 7-day forecast. Plenty\nof time to dry out fallowing all the rain. Temperatures during \nthe second half of the week will remain steady near to slightly \nbelow normal and then heading into the weekend temperatures are \nlikely to trend warmer as the ridging builds into the west. Most \nlower deserts may see high temperatures return to the low and \npossibly even mid 80s.",
